  "files": {},
  "metadata": {
    "title": "ViT: patches become tokens; CLIP aligns image\u2013text",
    "description": "ViT divides an image into non-overlapping patches, projects them to token embeddings, adds a CLS token and positions, then uses a standard Transformer encoder. CLIP uses separate image and text encoders with contrastive training so matched pairs score higher than mismatched pairs, enabling zero-shot prompt matching."
  }
